    {
      "id": 107,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "nginx vs backend latency — where is the time actually going",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 74
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "p95 request duration: nginx (all traffic) vs backend vs nginx→backend (upstream wait)",
      "description": "The gap between the nginx and backend lines is nginx's own overhead (proxying, queueing) — nginx's line should sit at or above the backend's, never below. The third line isolates the time nginx spent specifically waiting on the backend, as its own measured number (nginx_vts_upstream_*) rather than inferred from the gap — and, unlike the first line, it only counts requests nginx actually proxied to /api/, not static asset serving too.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 75
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(nginx_vts_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{host!=\"*\"}[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "nginx (all traffic, incl. static assets)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "backend",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
